      "start": 0.53,
      "end": 2.71,
      "text": "Hey, nice to hear from you. How are you?"
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 10.06,
      "end": 16.19,
      "text": "That's a lovely thing to learn for them. The basic idea is collecting sets of tiles, a bit like rummy with tiles."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 20.95,
      "end": 28.15,
      "text": "Yes, mostly sets of three matching or in a row, plus one pair. You take and throw away a tile each turn until your hand is complete."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 33.14,
      "end": 40.46,
      "text": "Learn the three suits first, dots, bamboo and characters. The numbers on the character tiles are the trickiest, a cheat sheet helps."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 46.8,
      "end": 52.927,
      "text": "Most families love that you're trying. Ask your partner which rules they use, because they vary a lot between regions."
